# Flow template — copy this file to input/<name>.flow and fill it in.
#
#   cp input/_template.flow input/my-feature.flow
#
# A .flow is plain English: it is what you WANT the video to show. Nothing parses
# it mechanically. The author-demo skill reads it, walks the real app through
# the Claude in Chrome extension, measures every wait, and writes
# scenarios/<name>.trace.json. author.mjs then generates the executable
# scripts/<name>.demo plus its scripts/<name>.selectors.json sidecar:
#
#   input/<name>.flow  ->  scenarios/<name>.trace.json  ->  scripts/<name>.demo
#
# To run it, ask Claude:  "author a demo from input/<name>.flow"
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Delete these instructions when you are done.

# ---- header ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Short id. Becomes the .trace.json / .demo / output file names.
name: my-feature

# One line: what the video demonstrates.
description: show how a user does X in the app

# Which deployment to record against: a file in targets/ (claude-ai, local-app,
# or your own copy of signed-in.json). Credentials never go in this file.
target: claude-ai

# Optional title cards, rendered by cards.mjs. Format: "Headline | Subhead".
# Both lines appear on the card and are read aloud. Delete a line to skip it.
intro: Product name | One sentence on what this demo shows
outro: Thanks for watching | Where to learn more

# ---- steps -----------------------------------------------------------------
# One step per line, in order. Write them the way you would explain the flow to
# a colleague. Useful shapes:
#
#   Open <page or screen>
#   Click <the thing, described by what it says or does>
#   Type "<exact text>" into <the field>
#   Ask the assistant: "<exact question>"
#   Wait for <something to finish or appear>
#   Confirm <what the viewer should see on screen>   <- becomes narration + a check
#   Pause on <something worth lingering on>
#
# Say "Confirm ..." after each action whose result matters: it tells the author
# what to wait for and what the narration should say when it arrives.
# Anything that SENDS, CREATES, EDITS or DELETES live data is confirmed with you
# before it is done during the walk.

Steps:
Open <the starting page>
Click <the first control>
Confirm <what appears>
Type "<text>" into <the field>
Confirm <the result the viewer should notice>
